WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.810
One winter evening, someone leans on a gate.

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:07.970
The frost is spectre-gray: a ghost's colour.

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:10.710
Dead stems scratch the sky.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:14.370
Like strings of broken lyres, the poem says.

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:17.610
Everyone else has gone in to their fires.

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:24.870
Then the speaker looks at the land and sees a corpse stretched out, the clouded sky its tomb.

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:27.650
So what has died in this poem?

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:33.990
In this mission, you'll read Hardy's The Darkling Thrush as an unseen poem, with no notes.

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:40.670
You'll see how a simile and one long metaphor build the mood, and work out whose corpse this is.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:44.200
Your mission: find out what has died in this poem.
